-- The shapes the 2026-09-07 refuters showed the deprecation warning getting
-- wrong, one per finding (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1.2), each now pinned:
--
--  * an infix head is named by its keyword (`plus`), not by its first input;
--  * a function over its own type variable is a term, not "a type that could
--    be anything", and gets a <type> hole since a section GIVEN cannot bind
--    the type variable;
--  * a type variable the type never mentions does not withhold the line;
--  * a FOR ALL type is spelled without the article;
--  * an input written without a type leaves a <type> hole, never a gensym;
--  * a bare ASSUME with no type at all is asked for its type;
--  * an AKA on the head is named, since a GIVEN cannot carry one;
--  * a @desc above the ASSUME is mentioned, since it moves with it.
--
-- A keyword usable as a name (`LIST`) is quoted on the suggested line too,
-- pinned in jl4-core/test/DeprecatedAssumeSpec.hs rather than here: the
-- layout printer prints such a name bare wherever it stands, so a file that
-- declares one does not survive the prettyLayout round-trip this directory
-- is held to.

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
ASSUME a `plus` b IS A NUMBER

GIVEN t IS A TYPE
      x IS A t
ASSUME identity x IS A t

GIVEN u IS A TYPE
ASSUME age IS A NUMBER

ASSUME pick IS FOR ALL v A FUNCTION FROM v TO v

GIVEN n
ASSUME `is large` n IS A BOOLEAN

ASSUME w

ASSUME rate AKA `interest rate` IS A NUMBER

@desc the fee the court charges to file
ASSUME `filing fee` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 100

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE sum IS 1 `plus` 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `one more` IS w PLUS 1

#CHECK `plus`
#CHECK identity
#CHECK age
#CHECK pick
#CHECK `is large`
#CHECK w
#CHECK `interest rate`
#CHECK `filing fee`
#CHECK sum
